## 9. SECURITY & PRODUCTION QUALITY

Treat security as a fundamental requirement.

Implement:

- Server-side authentication.
- Server-side role authorization.
- Secure magic-link generation.
- Hashed invitation tokens.
- Token expiration.
- Single-use token verification.
- Encrypted sensitive database fields using authenticated encryption such as AES-256-GCM.
- Environment-based encryption keys.
- Secure session cookies.
- CSRF protections where applicable.
- Rate limiting.
- Input validation.
- File upload validation.
- Secure error handling.
- Audit logging.
- Tenant isolation.

Never:
- Expose database credentials.
- Expose encryption keys.
- Expose email provider secrets.
- Trust client-side role information.
- Return sensitive fields unnecessarily.
- Store passwords or credentials in plaintext.
- Commit .env files.
- Log authentication tokens or private credentials.

Use appropriate production security practices and document any infrastructure-dependent security requirements.

